<title>USA: Geon to report $15 mln pre-tax charge in Q2.</title>
<headline>Geon to report $15 mln pre-tax charge in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>AVON LAKE, Ohio 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Geon Co said Friday that it will eliminate more than 15 percent of the jobs at its corporate headquarters as part of an ongoing effort to reduce costs, resulting in a $15 million pretax charge in the second quarter.</p>
<p>But the company added that the smaller work force will result in annual savings of $11 million annually in 1988 and therafter.</p>
<p>Most of the job reductions will occur through a voluntary early retirement plan over the next 18 months at company headquarters in  Avon Lake, where 450 people work.</p>
</text>
